Border Fixed Color =
SWITCH (
    MAX ( 'MappedParameterTwo'[Category2] ),
    "EngagementCodeList", "#01B8AA",
    "AlphaCode", "#FD625E",
    BLANK () // falls back to elementBorderColor in the spec -- see below
)
// Optional: bind this to the ColorOverrideBorder field (rename for this
// visual -- the spec maps it to the internal BorderColorOverride role).
// Same SWITCH shape as category-fixed-color.dax (including the same MAX-
// not-SELECTEDVALUE composite-key constraint -- see that file's
// comments), but for the element's
// border/stroke instead of its fill -- most of the time you won't need
// this at all, since the spec's elementBorderColor param (defaults to the
// shared background color, #182231, per docs/design-system.md) already
// gives every element a clean, uniform border. Use this measure only if
// specific categories need to stand out with a distinct border color
// (e.g. flagging an outlier), leaving BLANK() for everything else so it
// falls back to elementBorderColor via the spec's isValid() check.
